Ambient draft: views
$Id: views.readme,v 1.2 2005/07/04 23:06:09 laire Exp $


Introduction:
-------------
Views are a custom representation of an URI. It can be a directory content
displayed as icons or as a list, it can be a picture, a mp3 file, etc.. They
are a subclass of viewclass which is an internal Ambient class itself subclass
of MUIC_Virtgroup.


Basics:
-------
- Identification: view needs to report which mimetype and which protocols they
support. This needs to be done early (before a view is actually used). It also
needs to report which modes it supports with a default mode, for example
iconview can display as icons, icons for all files and thumbnails

example:

iconview:
- supported mimetypes: internal/rootview, internal/directory
- supported URI protocols: file (it could support more protocols later on)

fastlist: (should be renamed as listview :)
- supported mimetypes: internal/directory
- supported URI protocols: file (ditto)

htmlview: (formerly known as V :)
- supported mimetypes: text/html, text/plain, image/gif, image/jpeg,
  image/png, image/xbm
- supported URI protocols: http, ftp, mailto


- I/O: views initiate their own I/O. There might be advanced I/O abstration
later on for them to use


Library calls:
--------------
All views are libraries and need to implement the following calls that Ambient
will use to gather informations it needs.

APTR AVIEW_GetClass(void):
- get a pointer to the view class.

struct TagItem * AVIEW_Query(void):
- returns a static tagitem with requirements and
  abilities of the class. Following tags are available:

  - AVIEW_Query_Version (ULONG)
        The version of the view.

  - AVIEW_Query_Revision (ULONG)
        The revision of the view.

  - AVIEW_Query_Copyright (STRPTR)
        A string containing some copyright informations.

  - AVIEW_Query_Info (STRPTR)
        A generic information string describing the view.

  - AVIEW_Query_APIVersion (ULONG)
        Specify which version of the API the view implements.
        The current implementation is version 1. If this tag is not specified
        it defaults to API version 1.

  - AVIEW_Query_HasPrefs (ULONG)
        Set this tag to TRUE if your plugin implements preferences support.
        Preferences support is not implemented yet.

  - AVIEW_Query_MimeType (STRPTR)
  		Specifies a supported mimetype (eg. "text/plain"). This tag can be
        specified multiple times if your view supports more than one mimetype.

  - AVIEW_Query_MimeExtension (STRPTR)
  		Specifies a supported file extension (eg. "txt"). This tag can be
        specified multiple times if your view supports more than one filename
        extension.

  - AVIEW_Query_Viewmode_Name (STRPTR)
  		Specifies a name for one of the view's display mode. This is not
        necessary if you only have one display mode. This name will be
        displayed in various places like a view's context menu. There can be
        multiple tags, the first one being the default viewmode. You must also
        supply a AVIEW_Query_ViewMode_RexxName or this tag is ignored.

  - AVIEW_Query_ViewMode_RexxName (STRPTR)
  		Specifies the ARexx name of the view display mode so it can be
        referenced through ARexx or built in commands. This tag goes in pair
        with AVIEW_Query_Viewmode_Name.

  - XXX: implement some program scanning hook or language scanning system




Methods:
--------
The following methods are sent to the view:

MM_View_LoadURI,
MM_View_Abort,
MM_View_Mode,
MM_View_Setup,
MM_View_Cleanup,
MM_View_Refresh,


The following methods can be sent to the superclass by the view:

MM_View_ReadArgs,
MM_View_SetWindowPosition,
MM_View_SetStatus,
MM_View_ContextMenuMerge,


The following attributes are gathered from the view by the superclass:


The following attributes are available for the view:

  - MA_View_ModeIndex [IS.] (ULONG)
  		Specifies the selected mode from the ones supplied by
        AVIEW_Query_Viewmode_Name/RexxName. 0 is the first.

